From 9a54472d5e0c09699b0c5fbaea5f00763fac6823 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <226450061+logdog2325@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:58:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 155/157] XD Netplay v1.7.4: Realgam, Realgam Classic, Pyrite
 and Phenac formats

Four new formats, all Orre shaped like Orre Colosseum: bring 6, pick 4,
double battle, the same pinned rules record (Lv100 preset slot 3 or Lv50
slot 2, entries 4, entry mode 0 so the game's pick flow runs) with every
in-game clause on, and the same app-side Species Clause, Item Clause and
Soul Dew ban.

Realgam (id 10, "[Realgam] ", Lv 100): a team may bring up to two of
Mewtwo, Mew, Lugia, Ho-Oh, Celebi, Kyogre, Groudon, Rayquaza, Jirachi and
Deoxys, counted over all six. Refusal: "3 Restricted or Mythical Pokemon,
the limit is 2".

Realgam Classic (id 11, "[Realgam-C] ", Lv 100): the same, limit one.

Pyrite (id 12, "[Pyrite] ", Lv 50, cap 50): every Pokemon must have an
evolution whose National dex number is in its own generation block (1-151,
152-251, 252-386). Middle stages qualify. Refusal: "banned species:
Scyther (no evolution in its own generation)".

Phenac (id 13, "[Phenac] ", Lv 50, cap 50): Pyrite's rule and no
pre-evolution from the same or an earlier generation, plus Metapod,
Kakuna, Silcoon and Cascoon. Pikachu, Clefairy, Jigglypuff and Marill are
refused their listed baby and egg moves.

gen3data.json has no evolution data, so FormatRules carries the 184 Gen 1-3
evolution edges as a constant table and computes both species rules from
it once, on first use. Each format has an allow-list array for species
admitted by name; Pyrite's is empty for now.

Every picker lists them after Hoenn Limited, before Multi and Free, from
the shared-core list (Android included, through the existing JNI list).
The launcher tooltip and the Android format hints describe them.
